				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Bounded contract and owners\nCatalystFoundation owns CFConfiguration (BVC-Foundation-Config-Core), generic composition of Magritte-described objects and Atelier GT UI. Configuration specialises generic composition. CatalystRuntime owns CRConfiguration (BVC-Runtime-Configuration), Runtime semantic validation and fail-closed CRConfigurationSnapshot isolation. See {{gtPage:Foundation configuration authoring in Atelier|db=731asfxqhyhdr96k6wo9yxnzv}} (UID 7qwpgbmci583eb5iq84j8io16), {{gtPage:Runtime design contract|db=760mc3rkot5pkhueq2jxjz5gt}} and CatalystRuntime/runtime/Runtime-Ownership-and-Vocabulary.md (read-only evidence).\n\nRequired consolidation: CRConfiguration subclasses CFConfiguration and inherits one parent slot, basic ancestry and initialization. Preserve CR defaultWithParent: dispatch through default (CF uses new), withParent:, first-ancestor search APIs, semantic validation and Runtime snapshot copying. No invented parent-tree restrictions, no substitution of the planner copier for Runtime snapshots. Headless models acquire no GT UI dependencies. CFConfiguration>>asAtelier and >>descriptionContainerDetail: remain extensions owned by BVC-Foundation-Config-UI-Core; after consolidation Runtime configuration inherits these presentation effects in GT.\n\nPlacement discovery, simulation and rejection of newly introduced validation errors MUST remain supported. Smooth, intent-revealing Motion animation is a CORE Atelier requirement, not optional polish. Existing editor/animation paths must not be removed or degraded before accepted equivalent coverage. This bounded model change cannot establish whole Atelier completion.\n\nNext-slice gap: immediate CFConfigurationPlacement relation parent hooks are not integrated with generic CFMaMemento staged relations. Do not represent immediate relation mutation as staged/reset-safe composition. No broad staged-relation integration in this increment."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
